  "text": "Science & Exploration ExoMars Has life ever existed on Mars? The mission The ExoMars programme comprises two missions: the first – the Trace Gas Orbiter – launched in 2016 while the second, carrying the Rosalind Franklin rover, will target launch in 2028. Together they will address the question of whether life has ever existed on Mars. 1st European rover 2 m rover drill depth 70m/sol driving on Mars Latest All Stories Videos Images Image Science & Exploration ExoMars ramps put up with cold, shaking and vacuum 21/07/2026 128 views 2 likes View Story Science & Exploration ExoMars rover targets vast bed of clay in search for life 04/06/2026 4252 views 57 likes Read Video 00:00:27 Science & Exploration Landing sideways 18/05/2026 1464 views 28 likes Play Image Enabling & Support Sensitive and sturdy 07/05/2026 2096 views 50 likes View Image Enabling & Support The great parachute bake-out 30/04/2026 5182 views 71 likes View Video 00:02:02 Science & Exploration Baking a parachute for Mars 30/04/2026 2227 views 42 likes Play Story Science & Exploration The radiation paradox: why solar maximum is the safest time… 09/03/2026 4830 views 64 likes Read Story Science & Exploration ESA’s Mars orbiters watch solar superstorm hit the Red Plan… 05/03/2026 11782 views 62 likes Read Video 00:00:31 Science & Exploration Legs made for a Mars landing 21/01/2026 2721 views 32 likes Play Story Science & Exploration Legs made for a Mars landing 21/01/2026 5842 views 39 likes Read Image Science & Exploration Rolling out the red carpet for Mars 03/12/2025 2075 views 23 likes View Story Space Safety ESA pinpoints 3I/ATLAS’s path with data from Mars 14/11/2025 154004 views 217 likes Read Image Science & Exploration Swoosh! 06/11/2025 11315 views 113 likes View Video 00:02:04 Science & Exploration Sample processing 03/10/2025 1651 views 26 likes Play Video 00:02:13 Science & Exploration ExoMars parachute high-altitude drop test 21/07/2025 3909 views 50 likes Play More items Story Scie